Z||000012||87FieroGTx||11-15-2001||09:23 PM|||| I love this kit but it requires a 12" frame stretch <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> If I was going to stretch It I would get a Warlock Diablo with SE side vents.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/photo4.jpg"> <P>Sweet)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/photo3_1.jpg"> <P>Hehe.. Look at the stock BRAKES!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/knotts13.jpg"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seeng.jpg"> <P>And you can fit a longitudinal V8(any one from this stock L98 to an LS6 some people have actually put in 300-500hp BMW V12's OH.. you can also use a Porsche 4 speed that will take up to 750hp or a Porsche 5 speed rated to 400.<P> The red one up top actually has a REAL Diablo engine in it, the only way the ppl could tell it was a fake were the brakes. I have more Pix if anyone cares.<P><BR>I could go on for hours but CSI is on !!!!!! GtG<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||JB||11-15-2001||09:39 PM||||Thanks for the pics,87fieroGTx,  I too am a admirer of the Lambo Diablo.  It is actually one of my favorite cars if not the favorite.  My main reason for requesting pics of the porsche rebodies is because I am building one.  Isn't great that we can feel a kinship to these kind of supercars because of design similarities even though we drive cars that are over a decade old.  I love it!||||reg||1
